B.a8t=new A.c5("What is this?","AW139 CAT A take-off and landing performance from RFM Supplement 12 (Rev. 33; above 6400 kg Supplements 50 and 90 for Clear Area): weight-altitude-temperature (WAT) limit, rejected and continued take-off distances, landing distances, and the Path 1 / Path 2 climb gradients. Every value is read from the RFM charts themselves. The RFM remains the authority.",null)
B.a8E=new A.c5("1 \u2014 Aircraft and atmosphere",'Enter the gross weight and air intake (Clean, EAPS OFF, EAPS ON or IBF), then OAT and pressure altitude. "From field altitude & QNH" works the pressure altitude out for you: field altitude + (1013.25 - QNH) x 27 ft/hPa, with QNH in hPa or inHg. The wind is optional: direction it blows from, speed and the take-off / landing direction; the head/tailwind and crosswind are worked out from them. The crosswind is only checked against the 20 kt CAT A limit. kg/lb, \xb0C/\xb0F and ft/m can be switched on each field.',null)
B.a8W=new A.c5("2 \u2014 Procedure","Every take-off and landing procedure is listed with whether your weight is in or out of the WAT limit, and the maximum weight. Tap one to see its results; procedures outside the WAT limit can still be chosen. Short Field has no landing procedure. The TDP / LDP height field (where the procedure uses a variable height) and the obstacle fields appear once a procedure is chosen.",null)
B.a9h=new A.c5("3 \u2014 Results","The status card shows whether your weight is inside the WAT limit. Below it are the RTO / CTO (or landing) distances, the Path 1 and Path 2 gradients with the vertical speed at the chart airspeed, and the horizontal distance to gain the charted height. Warnings list anything outside the charts.",null)
B.a9e=new A.c5("Obstacle","Where the TDP or LDP height can vary (not Clear Area or Offshore Helideck, which assume no obstacles), enter one obstacle: its distance from the take-off point along the take-off direction (for a landing, from the landing point on the go-around side), its height above the surface and the clearance you want. The calculator checks the engine-failure path against it, suggests the lowest TDP / LDP that clears it and draws the profile. Inside the CTO or balked landing distance the RFM gives no path shape, so the lowest height of that stretch is used. On Back Up and Confined Area take-offs you can also enter an obstacle behind the take-off point, under the backwards climb: it is checked against the RFM obstacle-zone table (Figure 4C-8 / 4D-8), which does not depend on the TDP.",null)
B.a8T=new A.c5("Charts","Tap the chart icon on a result to open the RFM page with the red reading path: up from the axis, across, then down to the result, like the small diagram on each chart. The inputs sit beside the chart (below it on a phone), so you can change them and watch the path move. Pinch or Ctrl + wheel to zoom.",null)
B.a8q=new A.c5("PDF and saved scenarios","Download or Share builds one report with a summary page and one page for each chart used, for both take-off and landing with the same conditions. The bookmark icon saves the current flight conditions under a name so you can load them again (on a phone these actions are under the three-dot menu).",null)
